{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-luk-19-1","title":"Luke 19:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Of Zacchaeus a publican. 11 The ten pieces of money. 28 Christ rides into Jerusalem with triumph; 41 weeps over it; 45 drives the buyers and sellers out of the temple; 47 teaching daily in it. The rulers seek to destroy him, but fear the people.</p>\n<p>Jericho. Jos 2:1; 6:1-25,26,27; 1Ki 16:34; 2Ki 2:18-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-2","title":"Luke 19:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the chief.[Architelones ,] rather, \"a chief publican,\" or tax gatherer. Probably Zacchaeus, who appears from his name to have been a Jew, farmed the revenue of the district around Jericho, having others under him, who either rented of him smaller portions, or were employed as servants to collect the taxes.</p>\n<p>and he. 18:24-27; 2Ch 17:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-3","title":"Luke 19:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>he sought. 9:7-9; 23:8; Joh 12:21 because. 12:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-4","title":"Luke 19:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>climbed. 5:19 a sycamore. 1Ki 10:27; 1Ch 27:28; Isa 9:10; Am 7:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-5","title":"Luke 19:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>he looked. Ps 139:1-3; Eze 16:6; Joh 1:48; 4:7-10 Zacchaeus. Ec 9:10; 2Co 6:1 for. 10; Ge 18:3-5; 19:1-3; Ps 101:2,3; Joh 14:23; Eph 3:17; Heb 13:2 Re 3:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-6","title":"Luke 19:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>he. 2:16; Ge 18:6,7; Ps 119:59,60; Ga 1:15,16 joyfully. 5:29; Isa 64:5; Ac 2:41; 16:15,34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-7","title":"Luke 19:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>they all. 5:30; 7:34,39; 15:2; 18:9-14; Mt 9:11; 21:28-31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-8","title":"Luke 19:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Behold. 3:8-13; 11:41; 12:33; 16:9; 18:22,23; Ps 41:1; Ac 2:44-46; 4:34,35 2Co 8:7,8; 1Ti 6:17,18; Jas 1:10,11 by false. 3:14; Ex 20:16 I restore. Ex 22:1-4; Le 6:1-6; 1Sa 12:3; 2Sa 12:6; Pr 6:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-9","title":"Luke 19:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>unto him.Rather, as Elsner renders [pros autou ,] concerning him; for our Lord speaks of him in the third person.</p>\n<p>This day. 2:30; 13:30; Joh 4:38-42; Ac 16:30-32; 1Co 6:9-11; 1Pe 2:10 forsomuch. 13:16; Ro 4:11,12,16; Ga 3:7,14,29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-10","title":"Luke 19:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>5:31,32; 15:4-7,32; Eze 34:16; Mt 1:21; 9:12,13; 10:6; 15:24; 18:11 Ro 5:6; 1Ti 1:13-16; Heb 7:25; 1Jo 4:9-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-11","title":"Luke 19:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>they thought. 17:20; Ac 1:6; 2Th 2:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-12","title":"Luke 19:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>A certain. Mt 25:14-30; Mr 13:34-37 a far. 20:9; 24:51; Mt 21:38; Mr 12:1; 16:19; Ac 1:9,10 to. Mt 28:18; Joh 18:37; 1Co 15:25; Eph 1:20-23; Php 2:9-11; 1Pe 3:22 and. Ac 1:11; 17:31; Heb 9:28; Re 1:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-13","title":"Luke 19:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>his. Mt 25:14; Joh 12:26; Ga 1:10; Jas 1:1; 2Pe 1:1 delivered. Mt 25:15; Ro 12:6-8; 1Co 12:7-11,28,29; 1Pe 4:9-11 pounds.\"Mina, here translated a pound, is 12� oz., which, according to 5s. the ounce, is 3�. 2s. 6d.\"</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-14","title":"Luke 19:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>27; 1Sa 8:7; Ps 2:1-3; Isa 49:7; Zec 11:8; Joh 1:11; 15:18,23,24 Ac 3:14,15; 4:27,28; 7:51,52</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-15","title":"Luke 19:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>having. Ps 2:4-6 money. Gr. silver, and so. 23 that he. 12:48; 16:2-13; Mt 18:23-35; 25:19; Ro 14:10-12; 1Co 4:1-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-16","title":"Luke 19:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Lord. 1Ch 29:14-16; 1Co 15:10; Col 1:28,29; 2Ti 4:7,8; Jas 2:18-26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-17","title":"Luke 19:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Well. Ge 39:4; 1Sa 2:30; Mt 25:21; Ro 2:29; 1Co 4:5; 2Ti 2:10; 1Pe 1:7; 5:4 been. 16:10; 22:30; Mt 25:21; Re 2:26-29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-18","title":"Luke 19:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>thy. Mt 13:23; Mr 4:20; 2Co 8:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-19","title":"Luke 19:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Be. Isa 3:10; 1Co 3:8; 15:41,42,58; 2Co 9:6; 2Jo 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-20","title":"Luke 19:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Lord. 13; 3:9; 6:46; Pr 26:13-16; Mt 25:24; Jas 4:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-21","title":"Luke 19:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>I feared. Ex 20:19,20; 1Sa 12:20; Mt 25:24,25; Ro 8:15; 2Ti 1:7; Jas 2:10 1Jo 4:18 because. 1Sa 6:19-21; 2Sa 6:9-11; Job 21:14,15; Eze 18:25-29; Mal 3:14,15 Ro 8:7; Jude 1:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-22","title":"Luke 19:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Out. 2Sa 1:16; Job 15:5,6; Mt 12:37; 22:12; Ro 3:19 Thou knewest. Mt 25:26,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-23","title":"Luke 19:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Wherefore. Ro 2:4,5 usury. Ex 22:25-27; De 23:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-24","title":"Luke 19:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Take. 12:20; 16:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-25","title":"Luke 19:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Lord. 16:2; 2Sa 7:19; Isa 55:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-26","title":"Luke 19:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>That unto. 8:18; Mt 13:12; 25:28,29; Mr 4:25; Joh 5:1-3 and from.That is, the poor man, who possesses but little.</p>\n<p>16:3; 1Sa 2:30; 15:28; 2Sa 7:15; Ps 109:8; Eze 44:12-16; Mt 21:43 Ac 1:20; 2Jo 1:8; Re 2:3; 3:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-27","title":"Luke 19:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>14,42-44; 21:22,24; Nu 14:36,37; 16:30-35; Ps 2:3-5,9; 21:8,9 Ps 69:22-28; Isa 66:6,14; Na 1:2,8; Mt 21:37-41; 22:7; 23:34-36 1Th 2:15,16; Heb 10:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-28","title":"Luke 19:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>he went. 9:51; 12:50; 18:31; Ps 40:6-8; Mr 10:32-34; Joh 18:11; Heb 12:2 1Pe 4:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-29","title":"Luke 19:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>when. Mt 21:1-11; Mr 11:1-11; Joh 12:12-16 Bethany. 37; 21:37; 22:39; 24:50; Zec 14:4; Ac 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-30","title":"Luke 19:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>32; 22:8-13; 1Sa 10:2-9; Joh 14:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-31","title":"Luke 19:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>the Lord. Ps 24:1; 50:10-12; Mt 21:2,3; Mr 11:3-6; Ac 10:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-34","title":"Luke 19:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Zec 9:9; Joh 10:35; 12:16; 2Co 8:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-35","title":"Luke 19:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>they cast. 2Ki 9:13; Mt 21:7; Mr 11:7,8; Joh 12:14; Ga 4:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-36","title":"Luke 19:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>Mt 21:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-37","title":"Luke 19:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>at. 20; Mr 13:3; 14:26 the whole. 7:16; Ex 15:1-18; Jud 5:1-31; 2Sa 6:2-6; 1Ki 8:55,56; 1Ch 15:28 1Ch 16:4-7; 2Ch 29:28-30,36; Ezr 3:10-13; Ps 106:12,13 Joh 12:12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-38","title":"Luke 19:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>Blessed. 13:35; Ps 72:17-19; 118:22-26; Zec 9:9; Mt 21:9; Mr 11:9,10 peace. 2:10-14; Ro 5:1; Eph 2:14-18; Col 1:20 glory. Eph 1:6,12; 3:10,21; 1Ti 1:17; 1Pe 1:12; Re 5:9-14; 19:1-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-39","title":"Luke 19:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>rebuke. Isa 26:11; Mt 23:13; Joh 11:47,48; 12:10,19; Ac 4:1,2,16-18 Jas 4:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-40","title":"Luke 19:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>Ps 96:11; 98:7-9; 114:1-8; Isa 55:12; Hab 2:11; Mt 3:9; 21:15,16 Mt 27:45,51-54; 2Pe 2:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-41","title":"Luke 19:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>and wept. Ps 119:53,136,158; Jer 9:1; 13:17; 17:16; Ho 11:8; Joh 11:35 Ro 9:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-42","title":"Luke 19:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>If. De 5:29; 32:29; Ps 81:13; Isa 48:18; Eze 18:31,32; 33:11 in this. 44; Ps 32:6; 95:7,8; Isa 55:6; Joh 12:35,36; 2Co 6:1,2 the things. 1:77-79; 2:10-14; 10:5,6; Ac 10:36; 13:46; Heb 3:7,13,15; 10:26-29 Heb 12:24-26 but. Isa 6:9,10; 29:10-14; 44:18; Mt 13:14,15; Joh 12:38-41; Ac 28:25-27 Ro 11:7-10; 2Co 3:14-16; 4:3,4; 2Th 2:9-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-43","title":"Luke 19:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>the days. 21:20-24; De 28:49-58; Ps 37:12,13; Da 9:26,27; Mt 22:7; 23:37-39 Mr 13:14-20; 1Th 2:15,16 cast.Or, \"cast a bank\" or rampart [charax .] This was literally fulfilled when Jerusalem was besieged by Titus; who surrounded it with a wall of circumvallation in three days, though not less than 39 furlongs in circumference; and when this was effected, the Jews were so enclosed on every side, that no person could escape from the city, and no provision could be brought in.</p>\n<p>Isa 29:1-4; Jer 6:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-44","title":"Luke 19:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>lay. 1Ki 9:7,8; Mic 3:12 thy children. 13:34,35; Mt 23:37,38 leave. 21:6; Mt 24:2; Mr 13:2 because. 42; 1:68,78; La 1:8; Da 9:24; Joh 3:18-21; 1Pe 2:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-45","title":"Luke 19:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>went. Mt 21:12,13; Mr 11:15-17; Joh 2:13-17 sold. De 14:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-46","title":"Luke 19:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>Ps 93:5; Isa 56:7; Jer 7:11; Eze 43:12; Ho 12:7; Mt 23:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-47","title":"Luke 19:47","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":47,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":47},"content":"<p>taught. 21:37,38; Mt 21:23; Mr 11:27-33; Joh 18:20 the chief priests. Mt 26:3,4; Mr 11:18; 12:12; 14:1; Joh 7:19,44; 8:37-40; 10:39 Joh 11:53-57</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-19-48","title":"Luke 19:48","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":48,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":48},"content":"<p>could. 20:19,20; 22:2-4; Mt 22:15,16 were very attentive to hear him. or, hanged on him.[Kremannumi autou akouo ,] literally, \"they hung upon him hearing;\" which is beautifully expressive of their earnest attention, and high gratification.</p>\n<p>Ne 8:3; Joh 7:46-49; Ac 16:14</p>"}]}